  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the OpenSocrates instructions and repository notes, then inspect the starter and implement the backend within the 1,200-second window. I’ll keep all work local, run meaningful correctness checks, and stop any server I start.",
    "The starter is just a SQLite driver wrapper plus the legacy fixture producer; the acceptance contract is in `TASK.md`. I’m checking the installed controller’s decision path and the available local tooling before choosing the storage and transaction layout.",
    "The main consistency choice is settled: entries will be the source for historical reads, while current account rows support writes. Mutations will use an immediate SQLite transaction, so idempotency lookup, version checks, effects, and the saved response serialize together across processes. I’m implementing that now.",
    "The mutation paths are in place, including tenant-wide retry storage, sequential batch updates, holds, captures, and reversals. I’m finishing snapshot reads and migration verification now, then I’ll compile and exercise the HTTP contract against temporary databases."
